From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MicroNUX <micronux@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 21:35:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/46] video: fbdev: settle backlight before stopping scanout

The Kit C display adapter accepts its brightness-off I2C write before the
backlight has become physically dark. Stopping the only valid DPI stream
immediately after that write exposes the JD9365 cyan no-video state during
fbcon and application transitions.

Keep the current valid frame scanning for the Waveshare-defined 100 ms
backlight-off interval, then quiesce the bridge and GDMA. The existing
unblank path already primes four complete frames while dark before restoring
brightness.

Signed-off-by: MicroNUX <micronux@example.invalid>
---
 drivers/video/fbdev/esp32p4-dsi.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/esp32p4-dsi.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/esp32p4-dsi.c
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/esp32p4-dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/esp32p4-dsi.c
@@ -92,6 +92,7 @@
 #define MICRONUX_FB_WRITE_GAP_US	2
 #define MICRONUX_SCANOUT_START_TIMEOUT_MS 500
 #define MICRONUX_SCANOUT_STABLE_FRAMES	4
+#define MICRONUX_BACKLIGHT_OFF_SETTLE_MS 100
 
 #define MICRONUX_TOUCH_ADDRESS_PRIMARY	0x5d
 #define MICRONUX_TOUCH_ADDRESS_BACKUP	0x14
@@ -741,6 +742,9 @@ static int micronux_fb_blank(int blank, struct fb_info *info)
 		ret = backlight_update_status(dsi->backlight);
 		if (ret || !dsi->scanout_active)
 			return ret;
+		/* Keep valid video present until the LEDs are physically dark. */
+		msleep(MICRONUX_BACKLIGHT_OFF_SETTLE_MS);
+		dev_dbg(dsi->dev, "backlight-off settled before scanout stop\n");
 		ret = micronux_dma_stop_reload(dsi);
 		if (!ret)
 			dsi->scanout_active = false;
